    "body": "> \r\n> \r\n> (In case someone else has the same problem)\r\n> I solved this by using `chocolatey`.\r\n> `choco install starship`\r\n\r\nHow did you do it? Because I installed it also but right away nothing happened. After that, added `eval \"$(starship init bash)\"` at the end of `~/.bashrc` and now I the error each time I launch Cygwin:\r\n````\r\n$ eval \"$(starship init bash)\"\r\n-bash: $'\\r': command not found\r\n-bash: $'\\r': command not found\r\n-bash: $'\\r': command not found\r\n-bash: /dev/fd/63: line 16: syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\\r''\r\n'bash: /dev/fd/63: line 16: `starship_preexec() {\r\n````",
