    "updated_at": "2021-09-06T09:02:43Z",
    "body": "My current setup looks like this:\r\n- I installed [PowerShell](https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell) to have a cross-plataform shell\r\n- I also install [Windows terminal](https://github.com/microsoft/terminal) to properly display symbols in windows. Note also the recommendations of starship [here](https://starship.rs/faq/#why-don-t-i-see-a-glyph-symbol-in-my-prompt).\r\n- I added the initialization line at the end of my profile for powershell as indicated in the [installation guide](https://starship.rs/guide/#%F0%9F%9A%80-installation) of starship.\r\n\r\nIn the process of installing everything, it was very useful to simply call `starship` to see if it was properly installed, before making the initialization access work. \r\n\r\nIf you go for \r\n```shell\r\nchoco install starship\r\nstarship\r\n```\r\nwhat do you get? do you see that starship is installed and prints the command options?\r\n\r\nI get the following\r\n```\r\nstarship 0.57.0\r\nMatan Kushner <hello@matchai.me>\r\nThe cross-shell prompt for astronauts. ☄🌌️\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n    starship.exe <SUBCOMMAND>\r\n(...)\r\n```",
